UNAVAILABLE means that the complete measurement cannot be recovered from
the supplied files. >= denotes a known lower bound, not a complete total.
Aggregated time uses durations rounded to the precision recorded in the logs.

DEFINITIONS AND COUNTING RULES
1. Wall-clock time is Upload completed.total_elapsed_ms / 1000, measured
   with the application's monotonic timer. It includes application overhead.
   Timestamp differences are provided separately because they can differ
   from the monotonic measurement. Server startup and idle time are excluded.
   For twolevel, no complete run timer is available. The sum of the selected
   eight sequential stage durations gives a lower bound on active wall-clock
   time. It excludes global-context generation, processing between stages,
   the abandoned original stage 6, and the interruption before resumption.
2. Cumulative aggregated time sums elapsed_s from distinct Responses request
   completed records, plus the recorded timeout budgets for cancelled Map
   attempts within the selected scope.
   Concurrent calls contribute separately. This measures cumulative client-side
   LLM waiting time, including polling and internal retries, not CPU/GPU time.
   Timeout cleanup and unlogged work are not recoverable, so affected totals
   are lower bounds. An internal retry's elapsed time is already included in
   its eventual completion record and is not added again.
3. Tokens are summed once per distinct Responses request completed record
   with numeric usage. Stage, hierarchy, and upload summaries are not added
   again. None means unknown, not zero. Completed repair/reprocessing calls
   are included even when their output was subsequently rejected.

